\title{flowcam: Download and Animate USGS Stream-Gage Camera Images}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.svg}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

A tidy interface to the U.S. Geological Survey (USGS) National Imagery Management System (NIMS) API (\url{https://api.waterdata.usgs.gov/docs/nims/overview/}), which stores and serves images collected by stream-gage cameras at monitoring locations across the United States. Provides functions to discover cameras by NWIS site number or camera ID, list and filter available images by date and time, download images at multiple resolutions, and assemble downloaded frames into animated GIFs or MP4 videos. Integrates with the 'dataRetrieval' package (\url{https://doi-usgs.github.io/dataRetrieval/}) to enrich camera records with watershed metadata (drainage area, hydrologic unit code, state, county) and to retrieve co-located streamflow, stage, or water-quality time series — enabling direct comparison of visual stream conditions with measured observations. API authentication uses the 'API_USGS_PAT' environment variable shared with 'dataRetrieval', so a single key covers both packages.

flowcam wraps the USGS National Imagery Management System (NIMS) API,
providing functions to discover cameras at USGS stream gages, list
available images, build image URLs, and download images to disk.
\subsection{Main functions}{
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=find_cameras]{find_cameras()}}: Query the camera catalog by site or camera ID.
\item \code{\link[=find_gage_cameras]{find_gage_cameras()}}: Same, enriched with NWIS site metadata via
\code{dataRetrieval}.
\item \code{\link[=list_images]{list_images()}}: List image filenames for a camera, with date filtering.
\item \code{\link[=build_image_url]{build_image_url()}}: Construct full S3 image URLs from filenames.
\item \code{\link[=download_images]{download_images()}}: Download images to a local directory.
\item \code{\link[=get_timelapse_url]{get_timelapse_url()}}: Get the timelapse video URL for a camera.
\item \code{\link[=set_usgs_api_key]{set_usgs_api_key()}}: Save your USGS API key to \verb{~/.Renviron}.
}
}

\subsection{Authentication}{

An API key is optional but prevents rate limiting. Register at
\url{https://api.waterdata.usgs.gov/signup/} and store your key with
\code{\link[=set_usgs_api_key]{set_usgs_api_key()}}. The key is read from the \code{API_USGS_PAT} environment
variable, the same variable used by \code{dataRetrieval}.
}
}
